-- title:
--   A power of an invariant unit lies in Jⁿ
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M' \ge 1$ is an integer with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Further, $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\,\xi = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` identifies it as $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and subgroup $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base ring $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field and fraction field $L$, and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$; `hAq` puts $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and `hξA` puts $\xi$ in the image of $A$. The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and, by `hj`, has Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function. Here $\varpi$ is a uniformiser of $A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$ (the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$). The ideal $y \subset C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   For $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, call an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ a *level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$* when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds, that is: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on the level subgroup attached to $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ such that the Laurent series of $p_g$ is nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i /(q\ell)}$, the coefficientwise image of the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \alpha$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \alpha$, where $\alpha =$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a local-structure input, quantified over all relevant points and summarised here) states: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$), every germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the global function $\varpi$ pulled back from $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` mapping to $z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the sense above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv$ `drinfeldForm q W` $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u)$, such that seven clauses hold: $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; such $\tau$ with in addition $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ act trivially modulo $y'$; for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'$ there are $\theta \in \mathrm{Aut}(S)$, $c \in W$ and $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $e$ and the action of $\tau$ on germs, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_{j_0}) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{i j_0})X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing linear forms $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ up to second order with $q \nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; for such a prime containing $X_0$ up to second order, a germ lies in its contraction exactly when all Laurent coefficients of the corresponding element of $C$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; and finally `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` lies in $C \subset K$ and is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0 \in A$, with $e$ sending the germ of the difference to the class of some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form is nondegenerate in the sense that for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$ the value $\sum_{i \le e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit.
--
--   Next, specific data are fixed: a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of `XFin` with image $z$ (`hy'`) which is supersingular (`hss'`) and whose ideal is $y$ (`hy'y`); and a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ with $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$, $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for these data, exactly the seven clauses listed above.
--
--   The centre $J$ is an ideal of $C$ and `hJ` defines it as the infimum of the family of ideals obtained, as $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, by pulling back along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } y')$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i\}$, i.e. the $\varpi_t$-chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the blow-up of $J$. The valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses on these objects are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; `hR2`, that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak m_W$, and that $f \in W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for any $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A \to k_A$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, through elements $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that these automorphisms preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the target of the specialisation of $\mathfrak m_W$ under some such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that any such $\tau$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, $O$ is a subring of $K$ and `hO` presents it as a localisation of another chart of the same blow-up: there are $t \in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_t := C[J/t]$ (the $A$-algebra generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\,t = i\}$) such that $f \in O$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_t$ and $h \notin P$, every element of $y$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$. Moreover $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`). The last hypothesis `hIgStab` is a stability statement: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that $V \cap L$ is the image of $A$, such that $\varpi$ lies in $V$ and in $\mathfrak m_V$, such that $C \subseteq V$, and such that some $c \in C$ has $p(c)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$, one has, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, that $f \in V$ if and only if $\tau f \in V$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $u \in C$ with nonzero image in $K$ satisfying the four conditions
--   (i) $u$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$: there are $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $w \in C$ with $u\,w = \varpi^k$;
--   (ii) $u$ is fixed by all attached automorphisms: $\tau u = u$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$;
--   (iii) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L$ the image of $A$ and with $\varpi \in \mathfrak m_V$ whenever $\varpi \in V$: if $j \in V$, if $p(j)$ lies in $V$ and is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$, and if $O \subseteq V$, then $u$, whenever it lies in $V$, is a unit of $V$;
--   (iv) for every such $V$: if $j \in V$, if $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p$ over $A$, and if some $f \in O$ does not lie in $V$, then $u$, whenever it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak m_V$;
--   there exist natural numbers $a \ge 1$ and $n \ge 1$ such that $u^a \in J^n$ and $\varpi_t^{\,n}\,(u^a)^{-1} \in W$, the inverse being taken in $K$.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra half of the analysis of the blow-up of the supersingular point $y$ along the centre $J$: an element of the chart algebra that is invariant under the attached level automorphisms, divides a power of $\varpi$, and is a unit exactly at the Igusa-type valuation rings dominating the end $O$ is placed, after raising to a power, inside a power of $J$ with matching order along the exceptional valuation $W$ of the $\varpi_t$-chart. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart), and its proof draws on [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
